The second paragraph delves into a more specific example of updating aggregate values from one vertex to another (P(1,4) to P(1,3)) in O(1) time and space complexity. It demonstrates the practical application of the UpdateNeighbor subroutine by showing how only one input point changes its residual sign during the transition between vertices. This paragraph is essential for understanding the efficiency gains achieved through this methodology but builds upon the foundation laid out in Paragraph 1.

The distribution reflects that while both paragraphs are important, the first paragraph carries slightly more weight as it introduces and sets up the problem, which is crucial to understand before delving into specific examples or applications.
